      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JUDGE JENNI (4) needed her first run back from a spell when finishing 3 lengths back from the winner in sixth here nearly 5 weeks ago. Both of her career wins have been over this trip, so she will relish the extra 200m, and from the pole, with Darmanin on board, will be hard to beat. SUMMIT (1) was beaten by a nose as the favourite fresh, then repaid those supporters by winning a fortnight ago by the same narrow margin. The blinkers are back on, and he is good enough to repeat the dose. WHO'S IN DEV (3) has raced her way back into some good form, and was only half a length from the winner when third as the favourite at Hobart last time out. The blinkers are on for the first time, and on her more favoured circuit here, she will go close to taking it out. RIPPINGTON (2) can mix his form, but the small field will suit, as will having Troy Baker in the saddle for the first time. Keep safe. COOL CONQUEST (6) was better when fourth at Hobart 10 days ago, so stick with him.",
